Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:01:38.516 --> 00:01:41.227
Mashiki, I--

00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:51.446
"February"

00:01:56.534 --> 00:02:01.539
"Surgery In Progress"

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:21.851
Is Mashiki okay?

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.146
She's all right. Her condition's stable now.

00:02:25.355 --> 00:02:28.608
It may take some time for
her to wake up, though.

00:02:28.816 --> 00:02:30.818
| see.

00:02:33.237 --> 00:02:35.531
But that's all I can tell you.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.326
You should go home.

00:02:42.455 --> 00:02:44.999
So Mashiki-san's all right?

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:47.585
Yeah, we don't need to worry about her.

00:02:47.794 --> 00:02:49.212
That's good.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.380
Yeah.

00:02:50.588 --> 00:02:53.049
What about Mishima-kun?

00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:54.884
| better keep an eye on him.

00:02:55.093 --> 00:02:56.761
Please do.

00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:00.098
| think he'll feel better with you around.

00:03:00.306 --> 00:03:03.685
Thanks. Bye.

00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:11.776
| told the class rep.

00:03:11.984 --> 00:03:14.278
Thanks for everything today.

00:03:14.487 --> 00:03:15.655
| appreciate it.

00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:18.074
It's fine.

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.869
"The Merman Prince"

00:03:30.503 --> 00:03:32.338
We should go to sleep.

00:03:32.547 --> 00:03:34.507
I'm turning out the light, okay?

00:03:34.716 --> 00:03:35.883
Sure.

00:03:52.024 --> 00:03:53.985
Towa, you awake?

00:03:54.193 --> 00:03:56.237
What's up?

00:03:56.446 --> 00:04:01.117
| told Mashiki I like her.

00:04:02.577 --> 00:04:04.078
What am I doing?

00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:10.251
| was so focused on myself, I didn't
realize what was happening to her.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:11.210
That's why--

00:04:11.419 --> 00:04:14.422
Nah. Don't overthink it.

00:04:16.716 --> 00:04:18.384
Fine, worry all you want.

00:04:18.593 --> 00:04:20.386
| won't, though.

00:04:20.595 --> 00:04:22.013
What's your problem?

00:04:22.221 --> 00:04:24.140
Night.

00:04:46.162 --> 00:04:48.873
Towa, I'm going to the hospital.

00:04:49.081 --> 00:04:51.626
Sure, good idea.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.503
See you later.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.715
Okay.

00:05:01.844 --> 00:05:06.849
"Outpatient Reception”

00:05:11.813 --> 00:05:12.855
You're...

00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:13.689
"Outpatient Reception”
You're...

00:05:13.689 --> 00:05:15.608
"Outpatient Reception”

00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:24.826
Please come in.

00:05:25.034 --> 00:05:26.994
Thank you.

00:05:27.203 --> 00:05:29.288
Excuse me.

00:05:41.592 --> 00:05:43.261
She's sleeping right now.

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:47.473
I'm sorry. You came all the way here, too.

00:05:50.393 --> 00:05:53.187
Have a seat.

00:05:53.396 --> 00:05:55.231
Thank you.

00:06:00.736 --> 00:06:02.613
Thank you for yesterday.

00:06:02.822 --> 00:06:05.324
You called the ambulance, didn't you?

00:06:05.533 --> 00:06:10.329
I'm sorry I didn't notice sooner.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.710
Don't worry about it.

00:06:15.918 --> 00:06:19.088
She was already straining herself.

00:06:19.297 --> 00:06:20.631
What?

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:35.271
Miharu was born with a weak heart.

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:40.318
She'd originally planned to take
some time off before summer.

00:06:40.526 --> 00:06:44.906
Her doctor recommended surgery.

00:06:45.114 --> 00:06:48.701
We were seeing how things
went while preparing for it.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:51.495
Surgery?

00:06:52.496 --> 00:06:58.544
| told my daughter that surgery would make
her better, and she should have it done soon,

00:06:58.753 --> 00:07:01.964
but she wanted to wait.

00:07:02.173 --> 00:07:07.136
It was the first time I'd seen
her express herself so strongly.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.768
Thank you for coming today.

00:07:13.976 --> 00:07:16.562
I'll let her know once she wakes up.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:48.904
Mashiki-san's in the hospital?

00:08:49.113 --> 00:08:51.532
Yeah. I'm worried.

00:08:51.741 --> 00:08:53.868
Can we visit her?

00:08:54.076 --> 00:08:57.997
| don't know. Should we ask?

00:08:58.205 --> 00:09:00.583
Sorry I'm late.

00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:02.626
It's fine.

00:09:02.835 --> 00:09:04.170
| was just talking to Aki-chan.

00:09:04.378 --> 00:09:05.880
Excuse the intrusion.

00:09:06.088 --> 00:09:06.756
Pudding.

00:09:06.964 --> 00:09:08.340
Pudding?

00:09:08.549 --> 00:09:09.800
Oh, this.

00:09:10.009 --> 00:09:11.886
We'll make it together.

00:09:12.094 --> 00:09:14.096
I'll show you how.

00:09:34.325 --> 00:09:36.410
Welcome.

00:09:36.619 --> 00:09:40.331
One hot milk tea and three cups of ice cream.

00:09:40.539 --> 00:09:43.834
That will be 712 yen.

00:09:45.628 --> 00:09:47.797
Excuse me.

00:09:52.843 --> 00:09:56.097
Mashiki, I'm opening the curtain.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.089
We should just barely have
time to stop by the hospital.

00:10:30.297 --> 00:10:31.423
Where's Mishima-kun?

00:10:31.632 --> 00:10:33.300
Already there.

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:35.511
You're visiting Mashiki-san?

00:10:35.719 --> 00:10:37.930
Sanagi.

00:10:38.139 --> 00:10:39.807
Here.

00:10:42.434 --> 00:10:43.561
Pudding?

00:10:43.769 --> 00:10:45.688
| heard she's in the hospital.

00:10:45.896 --> 00:10:49.692
If you're going to visit, share it with her.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.318
Hey!

00:10:52.903 --> 00:10:57.575
Have you always known
about Mashiki's illness?

00:10:57.783 --> 00:10:59.827
Honda-kun?

00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:10.421
You're not in the same class, but you
seem to know Mashiki pretty well.

00:11:10.629 --> 00:11:13.716
We're just worried about her.

00:11:14.967 --> 00:11:16.927
Yeah.

00:11:18.304 --> 00:11:23.893
It's not my place to tell you much,

00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:26.145
but we met at the hospital.

00:11:26.353 --> 00:11:28.981
My family used to go there.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:31.442
That's where I met
Mashiki-san and her friend.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.528
Mashiki-san's friend?

00:11:36.071 --> 00:11:40.075
Yeah. When we were little, the
three of us used to play together.

00:11:40.284 --> 00:11:43.871
We'd get together out of
the way of the adults.

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:47.499
There was me, Mashiki-san, and another...

00:11:52.046 --> 00:11:53.422
Oh.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:03.641
Here.

00:12:03.849 --> 00:12:06.143
Thank you.

00:12:06.352 --> 00:12:08.562
No, thank you.

00:12:08.771 --> 00:12:09.855
It's fine.

00:12:10.064 --> 00:12:12.358
Um, would it be all right if I came tomorrow?

00:12:12.566 --> 00:12:14.818
Of course.

00:12:23.994 --> 00:12:28.040
Mishima-kun, did you attend
Wakaba Kindergarten?

00:12:28.249 --> 00:12:28.916
Huh?

00:12:29.124 --> 00:12:31.126
| couldn't remember yesterday,

00:12:31.335 --> 00:12:36.924
but you look a lot like a boy who
used to be friends with Misora.

00:12:37.132 --> 00:12:39.093
Misora?

00:12:51.313 --> 00:12:52.940
What?

00:13:17.965 --> 00:13:19.508
Mommy, I'm ready.

00:13:19.717 --> 00:13:22.052
No! I'm going with you!

00:13:22.261 --> 00:13:26.807
Come on. You should rest today.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.480
Misora.

00:13:40.195 --> 00:13:41.196
That's great.

00:13:41.405 --> 00:13:42.489
Yeah.

00:13:42.698 --> 00:13:43.949
Are you bringing your book?

00:13:44.158 --> 00:13:46.368
I'm gonna read it!

00:13:47.953 --> 00:13:50.664
Mommy!

00:13:51.498 --> 00:13:54.293
Misora's over there.

00:13:54.501 --> 00:13:56.503
It's my mom.

00:14:00.549 --> 00:14:02.217
Don't run.

00:14:02.426 --> 00:14:04.511
Okay.

00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:10.100
Huh? Where's your book?

00:14:10.309 --> 00:14:12.811
| gave it away!

00:14:17.941 --> 00:14:19.943
Misora! Misoral!

00:14:20.152 --> 00:14:22.196
This way, please!

00:14:22.404 --> 00:14:23.197
Misora!

00:14:23.405 --> 00:14:24.948
Please calm down.

00:14:25.157 --> 00:14:25.741
Misora!

00:14:25.949 --> 00:14:27.159
This way, please.

00:14:27.159 --> 00:14:27.951
"Surgery In Progress"
This way, please.

00:14:27.951 --> 00:14:29.161
"Surgery In Progress"

00:14:58.857 --> 00:15:00.692
Welcome home!

00:15:00.901 --> 00:15:02.986
We're having hamburgers today!

00:15:03.195 --> 00:15:06.907
Sorry. Tell Mom I don't need dinner.

00:15:07.116 --> 00:15:08.742
Huh?

00:15:08.951 --> 00:15:10.494
Okay.

00:15:32.683 --> 00:15:36.311
That wasn't originally my book.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:40.482
There was a girl who read
it to me and gave it to me.

00:15:40.691 --> 00:15:42.234
It's an important memory.

00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:44.111
"The Merman Prince"
It's an important memory.

00:15:44.111 --> 00:15:44.319
"The Merman Prince"

00:15:44.319 --> 00:15:47.531
"The Merman Prince"
She's really special to me, too.

00:15:47.531 --> 00:15:48.115
She's really special to me, too.

00:15:48.323 --> 00:15:51.368
Mashiki, are you...

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.759
Hey, I'm here.

00:16:07.968 --> 00:16:10.220
Towa?

00:16:10.429 --> 00:16:13.223
You could've answered your
phone if you were awake.

00:16:13.432 --> 00:16:15.684
Sorry, I didn't notice.

00:16:15.893 --> 00:16:18.562
It's fine.

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:19.646
Here.

00:16:19.855 --> 00:16:21.732
Thanks.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:25.652
| talked to Sanagi today.

00:16:25.861 --> 00:16:27.571
The girl who gave you the book...

00:16:27.779 --> 00:16:28.489
| know.

00:16:28.697 --> 00:16:29.364
Huh?

00:16:29.573 --> 00:16:31.825
It was Mashiki Misora, right?

00:16:32.034 --> 00:16:34.578
Yeah.

00:16:34.786 --> 00:16:37.789
Towa, hear me out.

00:16:37.998 --> 00:16:41.668
| thought about it.

00:16:41.877 --> 00:16:45.255
| had important memories of her.

00:16:45.464 --> 00:16:47.841
That's why I'd been watching Mashiki Miharu.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:53.138
Without those memories,
| wouldn't have talked to her.

00:16:53.347 --> 00:16:57.559
We talked, had ice cream together, laughed...

00:16:57.768 --> 00:17:03.732
Without that, these feelings |
have now never would've surfaced.

00:17:10.072 --> 00:17:14.368
| like Mashiki Miharu.

00:17:14.576 --> 00:17:17.246
I've never seen you like this.

00:17:17.454 --> 00:17:20.999
Tell Mashiki when she wakes up.

00:17:21.208 --> 00:17:24.753
Tell her everything you feel.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:02.916
Hello.

00:18:03.125 --> 00:18:04.543
Hey.

00:18:05.502 --> 00:18:08.630
Young people are so full of energy.

00:18:09.798 --> 00:18:11.883
Welcome.

00:18:20.183 --> 00:18:22.102
I'm opening the curtain.

00:18:57.137 --> 00:19:00.390
I'm Mishima Haruki, second-year.

00:19:00.599 --> 00:19:03.352
| like to swim.

00:20:18.009 --> 00:20:20.804
Mishima-kun.

00:20:25.726 --> 00:20:27.269
Good morning.

00:20:27.477 --> 00:20:29.771
Morning.

00:20:34.526 --> 00:20:37.654
Do you want something to eat?

00:20:41.742 --> 00:20:44.202
| thought you'd want to eat when you woke up.

00:20:44.411 --> 00:20:47.539
But I didn't know what you'd want,

00:20:47.748 --> 00:20:50.834
so I bought a bunch of stuff
at the convenience store.

00:21:00.427 --> 00:21:03.555
Have you been here the whole time?

00:21:06.099 --> 00:21:08.310
| bought snacks, too.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.858
Huh? What's wrong?

00:21:15.066 --> 00:21:16.985
Should I call the doctor?

00:21:29.247 --> 00:21:31.374
| can't eat all this.

00:21:31.583 --> 00:21:33.418
What?

00:21:44.805 --> 00:21:48.517
I'm really glad you're okay.

00:21:50.227 --> 00:21:52.771
Excuse us.

00:22:10.455 --> 00:22:18.964
Another city light blinks out

00:22:19.172 --> 00:22:28.807
Seems I'm the only one
being left behind like this

00:22:29.015 --> 00:22:37.524
I leaned in close to the light
of the vending machine

00:22:37.732 --> 00:22:46.658
And bought something
other than my usual coffee

00:22:46.867 --> 00:22:51.329
I wonder if I can be myself

00:22:51.538 --> 00:22:57.377
From now on, and even further beyond

00:22:58.503 --> 00:23:07.470
Surely someday we'll come
to know sadness as love

00:23:07.679 --> 00:23:16.813
Reconnecting somewhere
and parting again, over and over

00:23:17.022 --> 00:23:30.577
Surely the day will come when we're
all too used to feeling joy

00:23:30.785 --> 00:23:37.125
Call that happiness

00:23:40.003 --> 00:23:41.880
"Next Time"

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:46.217
"Next Time"
March, the season of his and her beginning.

00:23:46.217 --> 00:23:46.426
"Next Time"

00:23:46.426 --> 00:23:51.348
"Next Time" I've never been able to forget
you since you stood next to me that day.

00:23:51.348 --> 00:23:51.556
"Next Time"

00:23:51.556 --> 00:23:57.729
"Next Time" I'll keep swimming toward you so
I can stand by your side and hear your voice.

00:23:57.729 --> 00:23:57.938
"Next Time"

00:23:57.938 --> 00:24:01.441
"Next Time"
So I can learn what this feeling is called.

00:24:01.441 --> 00:24:01.650
"Next Time"

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.861
